{"name":"Cola","hex":"#3c2f23","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cola","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Malvaceae – kola nut trees.","A taxonomic genus within the family Noctuidae – certain moths."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Columbia, South Carolina"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cola","blocks":[{"text":"Cola is a carbonated soft drink flavored with vanilla, cinnamon, citrus oils, and other flavorings. The name, however, comes from the kola nut, which imbues the beverage with the stimulant caffeine. A stimulating soda using kola appeared circa 1880 in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Glass_of_Cola.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Cola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cola"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Berry_cola_stand_Reuilly.jpg/500px-Berry_cola_stand_Reuilly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Berry_cola_stand_Reuilly.jpg/1280px-Berry_cola_stand_Reuilly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Berry_cola_stand_Reuilly.jpg/500px-Berry_cola_stand_Reuilly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bottles of Berry Cola, a soft drink produced in Indre, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerry_cola_stand_Reuilly.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0098_-_Coca-Cola_glass_bottle_%28Germany%29.jpg/500px-15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0098_-_Coca-Cola_glass_bottle_%28Germany%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikim